Subject: Remove the debug and experiment switches nothing sets

What this does
  Drops `QJS_REGVM_ASM`, `QJS_REGVM_RCCHECK`, `QJS_REGVM_DYNADJ`,
  `QJS_REGVM_ARGCHECK`, `QJS_ALLOC_STATS`, `QJS_DRC_NO_EAGER_LARGE` and
  `QJS_DRC_NO_BACKEDGE` and their branches, keeping the default path: the
  assembly dispatch core, the value-id shadow checker, the
  dynamic-adjacency counter, the arg-retarget self-check, the allocation
  counters and the two deferred-RC ablation switches are all gone, and the
  constructors that only built them go with them.

Why we need it
  None of the seven is set by any build or tool, and each leaves an
  alternative branch plus, for the larger ones, a self-contained subsystem in
  the source. They were one-off diagnostics.

What it adds
  No new API. Runtime only.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

